# FlowCharts (`.mmd` + `.guide.md`)

Full system: [Documentation/02_FlowCharts](Documentation/02_FlowCharts/), builder [build_nav_and_charts.py](automation/dashboard/build_nav_and_charts.py), open via `wfcharts` ([wfcharts.md](Documentation/00_System_Wide/wfcharts.md)).

## Hard gate — do not auto-create

**Never** create, update, or regenerate flowcharts unless the user **explicitly** asks (e.g. “add a flowchart for X”, “document this flow as a chart”, “update the auth flowchart”).

Do **not** add charts as a side effect of implementing features, writing plans, or editing base docs.

## What each chart is

Every chart is a **paired artifact** (same stem, same directory):

| File | Role | Edit? |
|------|------|--------|
| `{name}.mmd` | Mermaid diagram source | Yes — author this |
| `{name}.guide.md` | Plain-English explanation + copy-paste examples | Yes — author this |
| `{name}.html` | Diagram page (nav + embedded Mermaid) | No — generated |
| `{name}.guide.html` | Guide page | No — generated |

- Chart page links to **“Plain English guide & examples →”** only if `{name}.guide.md` exists.
- Guide page links back to the diagram and the index.
- **Always ship both** `.mmd` and `.guide.md` for a new chart (unless the user asks for diagram-only).

## Where to put files

Under `Documentation/02_FlowCharts/charts/`, mirrored by concern:

| Area | Path |
|------|------|
| Cross-cutting (auth, WS, errors, presence, …) | `charts/base/` |
| Match pipeline (cross-stack: Flutter + Dart + later Python) | `charts/match_flow/` |
| Dart backend | `charts/dart_backend/{http\|state\|module_registry}/` |
| Flutter | `charts/flutter/{state\|…}/` |

Use **kebab-case** stems: `security-auth-flow.mmd`, `state-ws-routing-flow.mmd`.

Nav labels and titles come from the stem (`state-ws-routing-flow` → “State Ws Routing Flow”). Prefer a clear `-flow` suffix when it fits existing charts.

## Workflow (when user asks)

1. **Scope the logic** — read the real code/docs; one chart = one coherent flow (not a dump of the whole codebase).
2. **Write `{name}.mmd`** — Mermaid `flowchart` (usually `TD` / `LR`). Prefer subgraphs for layers/steps. Keep node labels short; put detail in the guide. Do **not** embed `%%{init:…}%%` (shared theme is injected at build if present).
3. **Write `{name}.guide.md`** — see guide shape below. First line is `# Title` (builder strips it; template owns the H1).
4. **Regenerate** from project root:
   ```bash
   python3 automation/dashboard/build_nav_and_charts.py
   ```
5. **Optional:** if a matching `Documentation/03_Base/*.md` exists and the user wants discoverability, add a one-line **Chart + plain English guide** link to the generated `.html` / `.guide.html` (same pattern as `ERROR_SYSTEM.md`, `WS_SYSTEM.md`).

Do not hand-edit generated `.html` or invent parallel chart trees outside `02_FlowCharts/charts/`.

## Guide shape (plain English)

Match existing guides (`error-handling-flow.guide.md`, `state-ws-routing-flow.guide.md`):

1. **Lead** — what the chart shows in one short paragraph (no jargon wall).
2. **Concepts** — tables or short sections for tiers, actors, or decision points.
3. **Step-through** — numbered path matching the diagram left→right / top→bottom.
4. **Copy-paste examples** — real snippets (Dart/Python/curl) a reader can try.
5. **Try it locally** — how to exercise the flow in this repo when practical.
6. **Related** — links to sibling charts (`.html`) and canonical docs under `03_Base/`.

Guide markdown subset supported by the builder: `#`/`##`/`###`, paragraphs, lists, fenced code, tables, `**bold**`, `` `code` ``, `[text](href)`.

## Chart quality

- Trace **actual** modules/files/APIs named in the repo; avoid fictional boxes.
- Prefer flow of control / data over class-hierarchy dumps.
- Split oversized topics into sibling charts (e.g. WS system vs Flutter reconnect) and cross-link in guides.

## Before finishing

- [ ] User explicitly requested the chart
- [ ] `.mmd` + `.guide.md` co-located under the right `charts/…` folder
- [ ] `python3 automation/dashboard/build_nav_and_charts.py` run; new chart appears in `index.html` nav
- [ ] No manual edits to generated HTML as the source of truth
